{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"agent_message","text":"Profiling found the main remaining avoidable cost: batched matmul silently makes contiguous copies of Q, K, and V because token-major storage interleaves heads. I’m fusing rotary with a cu-seqlens-aware repack into sequence/head-major storage. This preserves exact Q/K/V values, removes three hidden copies per attention batch, and still uses the same rocBLAS GEMMs and PyTorch softmax."}}
