{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"agent_message","text":"The padding bug was an operand-promotion mismatch: Triton had rounded the scale constant to BF16 before multiplying. Promoting scores to FP32 first makes scaled scores and softmax bit-identical. The padded path now has 100% tolerance match in every representative case.\n\nI’m integrating it only for mixed lengths and caching the tiny cu-seqlens descriptor for repeated calls to the same immutable tensor. The GPU kernels still read `cu_seqlens` every invocation; the cache only avoids repeating the host synchronization used to choose launch geometry, and is invalidated by tensor identity or mutation version."}}
